A||||3||extinct||high idle/code 35||||1||
Z||000000||extinct||10-22-2001||10:53 PM||||I have an 88 2.8 with about 35,000 miles.  The car starts fine but the idle stays up around 1500 rpm for a long long time, then when the car is fully warmed up it will slowly drop to about 1200 rpm.  When at idle for more than 60 seconds the check engine light comes on, then goes off when you resume driving.<P>Checked the codes, only one was #35 for idle air control.  I took it out and cleand it with tbi spray and then the tbi was sprayed too.  This did not help.  <P>1. Should I go ahead and replace the IAC valve? Anyone have a gm part # for this?<P>2. Can the EGR cause this, and if so how do I check it for leakes?<P>3.  Can the O2 sensor also cause the hight idle?<P>Thanks!  I will keep you posted.<P>extinct||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||10-23-2001||02:00 AM||||A cracked EGR tube can be the culprit. I have replace broken ones on both 88 GT's I have owned. You can test it by spraying carb cleaner at the ends of the tube while the engine is running. If the idle drops you have a crack.<P>Hope this helps,<BR>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000002||Fierozilla||10-23-2001||02:09 AM||||99% of the time when it throws an idle air control code, thats not the problem. Thats the cars only real way of telling you that theres a vacuum leak. Most of the time it is the EGR tube like mentioned above, but it could be anything. There are mazes of vacuum lines running all over the engine. It can sometimes be a pain tracking it down.<BR>1200 rpm isnt too bad...average in park/neutral is around 900-950 (it usually bounces back and forth) and around 750-800 in drive.<BR>Also you may want to look at your engine while its running at night w/no lights.....see if your exhaust manifolds glow. Thats usually another sign of a vacuum leak.||||reg||1
Z||000003||extinct||10-23-2001||11:45 PM||||Yep! I took the little dental mirror and sure enough there is a hair line crack on intake side.<P>Now anyone know where I can get an 88 tube fast!!!<P>Fiero store uses the stock one.<P>I am to scared to order anything from FOCOA<BR>(wait 4 weeks and may or may not get it)<P>What about IRM, anyone know how to order from them?<P>Thanks.<P>||||reg||1
